## AFTER, 18x45 external replay: outer iteration 2 re-solves the already-solved system; BiCGSTAB reports status 2 =
## Breakdown at 1.08e-11 (target rel 1e-10 of 4.5e-10 unreachable). 1.08e-11 <= rel 1e-10 x the first iteration's
## initial residual 6.75 = 6.75e-10, so runPicardLoop accepts it as an attained solve (max|dT| 2.3e-9 < 1e-8 -> Converged,
## part 2 above: 18x45 converged in 2 it); before that rule the production loop reported LinearSolveFailure here.
# part 1: production Picard loop replayed, sector 18x45x3, tolerance 1e-08, linear rel 1e-10
# it | linear residual | consistent residual | max|dT| | max adiabatic dTb | lagged adiabatic flux (hot half) | heat in | heat out | T L2 err | spread/Q
     linear solve: status 0, 152 iterations, initial residual 6.751e+00, final 4.544e-10
   1 | 4.544e-10 | 4.544e-10 | 4.963e-01 | 4.963e-01 | +6.363e+01 | 0.1470793157 | 0.1470793157 | 1.156e-07 | 6.952e-09
     linear solve: status 2, 34 iterations, initial residual 4.544e-10, final 1.081e-11
   2 | 1.081e-11 | 1.081e-11 | 2.290e-09 | 2.290e-09 | +3.208e-07 | 0.1470793144 | 0.1470793144 | 1.146e-07 | 2.877e-12  <- converged (returned)

## A first attempt at the loop change (skip the re-solve when the field already met the FIRST solve's linear tolerance)
## was rejected: it stopped cases run with a deliberately loose linear tolerance after one solve (HeatedCavity 80x80:
## L2 error 3.1e-4 vs 1e-6; TwoMaterialConduction 40/80: 1.2e-4 / 9.1e-3 vs 5e-6) -- they rely on the outer loop
## re-solving (refining) until max|dT| < 1e-8. The final rule keeps that loop unchanged and only accepts an attained breakdown.

